        <mxCell id="note126" value="&lt;div style=&quot;padding:8px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;ref&lt;/b&gt; Separate counterfactual replay: VIP orders/prepares on turn 6, is served on turn 7, becomes READY_TO_PAY on turn 8 and pays on turn 9. Its payment snapshot is 85. The remaining customers are also scheduled by the same priority rule. Final result: VICTORY, 5 paid, $64.50, satisfaction sum 389, average 77.80. Thus one staff-priority choice changes timing and satisfaction, while both runs still win.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;overflow=fill;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;strokeColor=#20252b;fillColor=#ffffff;">
